  "verses": [
    {
      "verse": "1",
      "en": {
        "text": "LORD, our Lord, how majestic is your name in all the earth! You have set your glory above the heavens!",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "耶和华—我们的主啊，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "耶和華－我們的主啊，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "2",
      "en": {
        "text": "From the lips of babes and infants you have established strength, because of your adversaries, that you might silence the enemy and the avenger.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "你因敌人的缘故，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "你因敵人的緣故，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "3",
      "en": {
        "text": "When I consider your heavens, the work of your fingers, the moon and the stars, which you have ordained,",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "我观看你指头所造的天，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "我觀看你指頭所造的天，",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "4",
      "en": {
        "text": "what is man, that you think of him? What is the son of man, that you care for him?",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "：人算什么，你竟顾念他！",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "：人算甚麼，你竟顧念他！",
        "footnotes": [],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "5",
      "en": {
        "text": "For you have made him a little lower than the angels, and crowned him with glory and honor.",
        "footnotes": [
          {
            "id": "f1",
            "text": "8:5 Hebrew: Elohim. The word Elohim, used here, usually means “God”, but can also mean “gods”, “princes”, or “angels”. The Septuagint reads “angels” here. See also the quote from the Septuagint in Hebrews 2:7."
          }
        ],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhSimplified": {
        "text": "你叫他比天使微小一点，",
        "footnotes": [
          {
            "id": "f1",
            "text": "- 8:5 或译： 神"
          }
        ],
        "crossReferences": []
      },
      "zhTraditional": {
        "text": "你叫他比天使微小一點，",
        "footnotes": [
          {
            "id": "f1",
            "text": "- 8:5 或譯：上帝"
          }
        ],
        "crossReferences": []
      }
    },
    {
      "verse": "6",
      "en": {
        "text": "You make him ruler over the works of your hands. You have put all things under his feet:",
